---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Chiropractic Grit"
  description="Terms of service governing use of Chiropractic Grit's EHR, scheduling, patient portal, and SMS messaging platform."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="page">
    <div class="container">

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="page-header">
        <div class="kicker">Terms of Service</div>
        <h1>Terms of service.</h1>
        <p class="header-copy">
          These terms govern your use of the Chiropractic Grit platform ("Grit"), including scheduling,
          SOAP notes, patient portal, secure messaging, and SMS notifications. Please read them carefully.
        </p>
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: March 31, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="legal-content">

        <section>
          <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
          <p>
            By creating an account or using any part of the Grit platform, you ("Provider," "Staff," or "User")
            agree to be bound by these Terms of Service and our <a href="/sms-terms">SMS Terms &amp; Privacy Policy</a>.
            If you are using Grit on behalf of a practice or organization, you represent that you have the
            authority to bind that entity to these terms.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you do not agree to these terms, do not create an account or use the platform.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Description of service</h2>
          <p>
            Chiropractic Grit is a cloud-based practice management platform designed for solo chiropractors
            and independent chiropractic practices. The platform includes:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Patient scheduling and appointment management</li>
            <li>SOAP notes and clinical documentation</li>
            <li>Secure provider-to-patient messaging (in-app)</li>
            <li>SMS notifications from Chiropractic Grit about your account (waitlist, onboarding, billing, platform updates)</li>
            <li>Patient portal for self-service access</li>
            <li>Billing and balance tracking</li>
            <li>Provider schedule and time-off management</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Grit is not an emergency communication system. Do not use it to send urgent or time-sensitive
            medical communications. Always direct patients to call 911 or go to the nearest emergency room
            in the event of a medical emergency.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Account registration</h2>
          <p>
            To access Grit, you must register with accurate information including your legal name, practice
            name, and a valid business email. You are responsible for:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Maintaining the confidentiality of your login credentials</li>
            <li>All activity that occurs under your account</li>
            <li>Promptly notifying Grit of any unauthorized access at <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a></li>
            <li>Ensuring that all staff users added to your practice account comply with these terms</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You may not share login credentials between users. Each provider and staff member must have
            their own account.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. HIPAA compliance & business associate agreement</h2>
          <p>
            Grit is designed to operate in a HIPAA-compliant manner. As a covered entity or business
            associate under HIPAA, you acknowledge:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Grit acts as a Business Associate when handling Protected Health Information (PHI) on your behalf</li>
            <li>A Business Associate Agreement (BAA) is included with all Grit Pro subscriptions</li>
            <li>You are responsible for ensuring your use of Grit complies with all applicable federal and state healthcare privacy laws</li>
            <li>You must not transmit unsecured PHI through channels not designed for it (e.g., SMS messages must not contain diagnoses, test results, or clinical details)</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The BAA is incorporated by reference into these terms. If you require a countersigned copy,
            contact <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>
            You agree to use Grit only for lawful purposes and in accordance with these terms. You may not:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Use the platform to store or transmit content that violates any applicable law or regulation</li>
            <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of the platform or other users' accounts</li>
            <li>Reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble any part of the software</li>
            <li>Use automated scripts, bots, or scrapers to access the platform</li>
            <li>Send unsolicited or spam communications to patients through any Grit messaging channel</li>
            <li>Use the platform for any purpose other than managing your chiropractic practice</li>
            <li>Resell or sublicense access to the platform to third parties</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Violation of acceptable use terms may result in immediate account suspension without refund.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Payment & billing</h2>
          <p>
            Grit Pro is billed at <strong>$99/month</strong> per practice. Billing terms:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Subscriptions are billed monthly in advance</li>
            <li>Payment is due at the start of each billing cycle</li>
            <li>Accepted payment methods include major credit and debit cards</li>
            <li>Failed payments may result in a grace period followed by account suspension</li>
            <li>All fees are in USD and are non-refundable except as required by law</li>
            <li>Grit reserves the right to change pricing with 30 days' written notice</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Add-on services (such as additional SMS phone numbers) may be billed separately
            as usage-based charges.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Cancellation & termination</h2>
          <p>
            You may cancel your subscription at any time from your account settings or by contacting
            <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a>.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period</li>
            <li>You retain access to the platform until the period ends</li>
            <li>No refunds are issued for partial billing periods</li>
            <li>After cancellation, you have 30 days to export your data before it is permanently deleted</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Grit may terminate your account without notice for:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Violation of these terms or applicable law</li>
            <li>Non-payment after the grace period</li>
            <li>Use that creates legal, regulatory, or reputational risk to Grit or its users</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Data ownership & portability</h2>
          <p>
            You own your data. Grit does not sell, rent, or share your practice data or patient information
            with third parties for marketing purposes. Grit may access your data only to:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Provide and improve the platform</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
            <li>Investigate abuse or security incidents</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You may export your data at any time from the platform. Data exports include patient records,
            appointment history, clinical notes, and billing information in standard formats.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. SMS communications</h2>
          <p>
            Chiropractic Grit may send SMS messages to you (the practice account holder
            or staff user) for purposes related to your Grit account. By providing your
            mobile number and opting in via the waitlist form, account onboarding, or
            in-app preferences, you consent to receive SMS messages from us, including:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Waitlist updates and early-access invitations</li>
            <li>Onboarding and account-setup instructions</li>
            <li>Trial-status, billing, and subscription notifications</li>
            <li>Platform status notices (campaign registration updates, downtime, etc.)</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Message frequency varies, typically up to four messages per month per
            recipient. Standard message and data rates may apply. Reply <strong>STOP</strong>
            to any message to opt out, or <strong>HELP</strong> for help. We will not sell
            or share your mobile number with third parties for marketing purposes. See
            our <a href="/sms-terms">SMS Terms &amp; Privacy</a> for full details.
          </p>
          <p>
            Practice-to-patient SMS messaging (appointment reminders, two-way patient
            texting) is a planned feature. When that capability ships, each practice
            will register its own SMS sender with the carriers, and additional terms
            governing patient consent, HIPAA-compatible content rules, and TCPA
            obligations will be presented to the practice at that time.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            Grit and its underlying software, design, trademarks, and content are the intellectual property
            of Chiropractic Grit and are protected by applicable law. These terms do not grant you any
            ownership interest in the platform.
          </p>
          <p>
            You retain all rights to your data, clinical content, and patient records. By using Grit, you
            grant us a limited, non-exclusive license to store and process your data solely to provide the
            services described in these terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
          <p>
            The Grit platform is provided <strong>"as is"</strong> and <strong>"as available"</strong> without
            warranties of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of
            merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement.
          </p>
          <p>
            Grit does not warrant that the platform will be error-free, uninterrupted, or free from security
            vulnerabilities. Healthcare decisions must not be made solely based on information processed
            through the platform.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Chiropractic Grit's total liability for
            any claim arising from or related to these terms or the platform shall not exceed the greater
            of (a) the total fees paid by you in the three months preceding the claim, or (b) $100.
          </p>
          <p>
            In no event shall Grit be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive
            damages, including lost profits, data loss, or business interruption, even if advised of the
            possibility of such damages.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>13. Indemnification</h2>
          <p>
            You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Chiropractic Grit, its officers, employees, and
            agents from any claims, damages, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising from:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your use of the platform in violation of these terms</li>
            <li>Your violation of any applicable law or regulation (including HIPAA and TCPA)</li>
            <li>Any claim by a patient related to your practice's communications or clinical decisions</li>
            <li>Any content you submit, transmit, or store through the platform</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>14. Governing law & disputes</h2>
          <p>
            These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, without regard to its conflict
            of law provisions. Any dispute arising from these terms shall be resolved by binding arbitration
            administered under the rules of the American Arbitration Association, except that either party
            may seek injunctive relief in a court of competent jurisdiction for intellectual property
            or confidentiality violations.
          </p>
          <p>
            You waive the right to participate in class action lawsuits or class-wide arbitration.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>15. Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these terms from time to time. When we do, we will update the "Last updated" date
            at the top of this page and notify active subscribers via email at least 14 days before
            material changes take effect. Continued use of the platform after the effective date constitutes
            acceptance of the revised terms.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you disagree with a material change, you may cancel your subscription before the change
            takes effect and receive a prorated refund for any prepaid unused period.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="contact-section">
          <h2>16. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about these terms, your subscription, or your data:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Email: <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a></li>
            <li>For HIPAA-related requests: <a href="mailto:support@chiropracticgrit.com">support@chiropracticgrit.com</a></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

      </div>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 52px 0 84px;
  }

  .page-header {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin-bottom: 52px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .kicker {
    color: var(--ember);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4.5vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .header-copy {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .last-updated {
    color: var(--subtle);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-content {
    max-width: 740px;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  section:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  li::before {
    content: '';
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--ember);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--ember);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: var(--ember-strong);
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .page {
      padding: 36px 0 64px;
    }

    section {
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      padding-bottom: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
